  "algorithm": "agiskill-sha256-v1",
  "notes": [
    "Verified by `node scripts/verify-skills-lock.mjs` (CI: .github/workflows/repo-operability.yml). Regenerate with --regenerate.",
    "The hashing algorithm is specified in packages/tools/skills/src/integrity.ts and reimplemented identically in apps/cli/src/skills.rs and scripts/verify-skills-lock.mjs.",
    "v1 of this file recorded computedHash values for ai-seo, programmatic-seo, remotion-best-practices, and seo-geo with no algorithm field. Those hashes are NOT reproducible: re-hashing the exact bundle bytes from d694f17b2 under agiskill-sha256-v1 yields different digests, and no generator for the v1 values exists anywhere in the repo. They were never verified against anything.",
    "Those four bundles were themselves deleted from .agents/skills in 5b14585dd, so their entries were also stale. They are dropped here rather than carried forward as unverifiable claims; git history retains the original values.",
    "The current bundles are original AGI Workforce instruction-only packages. Adding any skill under `roots` fails CI until it is locked with declared provenance.",
    "`audience` decides who may see a skill. `product` reaches the in-product Skills catalog served by apps/web/lib/services/skill-catalog-service.ts; `developer` is repository tooling for coding agents and never reaches an end user. Vendored bundles and skills describing work on this repository are developer. A skill with no audience is treated as developer at runtime and fails verification here."
  ],
